    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required `GET /api/owners/{id}` to return a read-only `membershipTier` field: `SILVER` when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise `BRONZE`.\n\nTwo changes, following the existing pattern already used for the computed `displayName`/`initials` fields:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema. The `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec at build time, so this gives the DTO its `membershipTier` getter/setter.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired the field via `@Mapping(target = \"membershipTier\", expression = \"java(toMembershipTier(owner))\")` and added a `toMembershipTier` default method implementing the rule (treats a null `namesakeCount` and a null/blank email as not qualifying \u2192 `BRONZE`).\n\n`namesakeCount` is already populated to 0 for a unique-named owner at creation time (`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`), so SILVER triggers correctly.\n\nResult: `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` for `AcceptanceTest` (both the SILVER and BRONZE cases), and the whole suite passes.",
